# RPM spec fragment for Tribalism (Fedora / RHEL / openSUSE).
# The full spec is generated by the packaging task; this captures the runtime dependencies that matter.

Name:           tribalism
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        The AI-assisted pen & paper game master
License:        Proprietary
URL:            https://github.com/gleethros/tribalism
BuildArch:      x86_64

# Runtime dependencies:
#  - java-21-openjdk-headless: the application is a JVM app.
#  - shadow-utils: provides the setuid-root newuidmap/newgidmap helpers REQUIRED for the AI agent's
#    rootless podman sandbox. On Fedora/RHEL shadow-utils is part of the base install, but we declare
#    it explicitly so the dependency is never accidentally absent. We ship podman/crun/conmon/
#    fuse-overlayfs ourselves — do NOT add them here. See packaging/README.md and
#    app.agent.sandbox.PodmanSandboxRuntime.
Requires:       java-21-openjdk-headless >= 1:21
Requires:       shadow-utils

%description
A desktop tool for pen & paper game masters with a 3D voxel map engine, live multiplayer sessions
over the LAN, and a sandboxed agentic AI game master that runs in its own rootless podman container.
